\section{Overview}


\section{Molecular representations in QSAR}

The success of machine learning hinges on the quality of input data. Although the quality can refer to noise, which the majority of our work is centered around, in this case we are talking about the type of input. Molecular representations provide different features with which QSAR models and noise detection techniques can be learned (Figure~\ref{fig:molecular_representations}). However, a potential bottleneck on larger datasets should be noted; the more complex the data structure, the greater the computational cost. For smaller datasets, the number of parameters is limited by the size of the training set, to prevent overfitting.

