The neighbor-based noise scores, sample removal, sample weighting, label smoothing and the recovery rate are defined in Chapter~\ref{chap:similarity}, ``Noise mitigation methods''.

The method needs a distance that picks the right neighbors, and neighbors with clean labels. Earlier sections of this chapter argue that the first condition fails, and the second fails whenever noise is spread over the whole training set. A large gap from the neighbors' labels can mean a noisy label, a noisy neighbor or the wrong neighbors, and the score cannot tell which. Activity cliffs also look like noise to such a detector (Chapter~\ref{chap:background}, ``Molecular similarity and activity cliffs'').

The exploratory study also used neighbors to clean labels, on 5,000 randomly chosen QM9 molecules (HOMO--LUMO gap, scaffold split) with Gaussian noise on the training labels at $\sigma = 0.3$ and $\sigma = 0.6$. Each cleaning method was judged by retraining a random forest on ECFP4 with clean, noisy and cleaned labels, giving the recovery rate, the share of the $R^2$ lost to noise that cleaning recovers (Equation~\ref{eq:recovery}). Neighbor-based scores compared each label with those of the molecule's $k$ nearest training molecules under Euclidean, Manhattan or cosine distance. Table~\ref{tab:code_input_neighbor_recovery} holds only the configurations built on a single representation; those built on an early hybrid are described below. This study is separate from the sample-removal study of Chapter~\ref{chap:similarity}.

With the neighbor-based scores used as sample weights at strength $\alpha = 0.1$, mean recovery was negative for every representation at both noise levels (Table~\ref{tab:code_input_neighbor_recovery}). Of all 860 cleaning configurations, 8 had positive recovery at both noise levels; 6 of these used a single representation, and 4 of those 6 were neighbor-based. Label smoothing toward neighbor or model estimates gave positive recovery in 5.0\% of configurations at $\sigma = 0.3$ and 0.8\% at $\sigma = 0.6$. Mean recovery was negative at every weighting and smoothing strength tried, from 0.1 to 0.7.

