Any representation that gives one fixed-length vector per sample can serve as a base representation (Section~\ref{sec:method:build}). The first version of the method used three molecular representations: PDV, ECFP4 and MHG-GNN. These three are now one small-molecule example among many. Every base representation is frozen: it is computed once from the raw input (a SMILES string, a sequence or a reaction) and is never trained on the labels.

% TODO: review, needs manual review
For each dataset we pre-selected at most ten base representations that carry different information and each showed some positive result on its own for the task.

To choose them, every candidate representation was first scored on its own with a gradient-boosted tree model \citep{ke2017lightgbm} under the dataset's grouped folds. Candidates were then compared by the Spearman correlation between their out-of-fold predictions, since two representations whose predictions correlate highly carry much the same signal. At most ten were then chosen by hand, looking at each candidate's own score next to these correlations and favoring representations that encode the input in different ways. Binding free energy has eight.% TODO: manual review -- [CLAUDE 2026-10-09] the H3K4me3 and TATA sentences (both cut) replaced; ddg_combined's stored pool has 8 representations (c02 rep_dims). Why it has 8 was not checked.

