This experiment asks whether the hybrid's gain holds on rare scaffolds as well as on common ones. Datasets above 2{,}000 samples are first reduced to about 2{,}000 by drawing whole scaffold groups with a fixed seed. Scaffolds at or above the 80th percentile of group size form the easy half, and the rest form the hard half. Each half gets its own search on each outer fold. The hybrid of a search on all the subset's training samples is also rebuilt and scored on each half. Three other splits (by heavy-atom count, label spread within a scaffold and feature spread within a scaffold) were run and are not reported here.

