The fourth question asked whether weighting features by their importance improves the hybrid and model training. In construction, ranking features by importance within each representation is what makes the hybrid work. In training, using the importance scores again adds little on small molecules and helps on some small antibody datasets, with no condition that works everywhere. Whether hybrids keep more of their performance under label noise, and whether their features stabilize noise mitigation, are the subjects of Chapters~\ref{chap:similarity} and~\ref{chap:noise}.

