The methods fall into the three groups of Table~\ref{tab:noise_terms}: noise detection, noise mitigation and noise-robust training. Chapter~\ref{chap:flaws} reported a small sweep of twelve published noise-handling methods on one dataset (Section~\ref{sec:lnl_motivation}), and this chapter expands that sweep. It also adds methods that select molecules by a known flag rather than a detector, such as a label sitting at an assay limit. The published methods have no place for these.

