Both halves of this thesis lead to the same advice. Before choosing a model, representation or LNL method, a practitioner should ask where the labels came from and what shape their noise is likely to have, then choose features for the task rather than take one representation whole. Since no single model or representation was best on every dataset in Chapter~\ref{chap:robustness}, and the best budget already differed between downstream models in the preliminary runs, the choices that vary by dataset should be searched and compared fairly.

